<Doc slug={slug} title="Configuration">
  <h1>Configuration</h1>
  <p>cortex selects the model. axon configures how that model is called and how the agent executes tools.</p>

  <h2>cortex config</h2>
  <p>Put defaults in <code>~/.config/cortex/config.yaml</code>. A <code>cortex.yaml</code> in the working directory overrides fields. <code>LLM_PROVIDER</code> and <code>LLM_MODEL</code> take precedence over both.</p>
  <pre><code>name: reviewer
provider: openrouter
model: deepseek/deepseek-v3.2
system_prompt: ./reviewer.md
explorer:
  provider: openrouter
  model: z-ai/glm-5.3-flash</code></pre>
  <p><code>--config PATH</code> disables the file cascade but still accepts environment overrides. A prompt can be inline text or a path, including <code>~/...</code>.</p>

  <h2>axon provider</h2>
  <p>Configure the endpoint and key in <code>~/.config/axon/axon.yaml</code>. Store the key in the adjacent <code>.env</code> file.</p>
  <pre><code>providers:
  openrouter:
    base_url: https://openrouter.ai/api
    api_key: &#36;&#123;OPENROUTER_API_KEY&#125;
    models:
      deepseek/deepseek-v3.2:</code></pre>
  <p>For an initial setup, see <a href="/cortex/docs/getting-started/quick-start/">Quick start</a>. MCP subprocesses may be configured under <code>mcp_servers</code> in the cortex file.</p>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
